cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use hetero1d in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "hetero1d: a one-dimensional semiconductor heterostructure solver"
abstract: >-
  hetero1d computes electron and hole states, optical transitions, gain, excitons,
  carrier statistics, LO-phonon scattering, tunnelling and self-consistent
  Schrödinger-Poisson solutions in semiconductor quantum wells, superlattices and
  arbitrary layer stacks, including strain, non-parabolicity, and electric and
  magnetic fields.
authors:
  - name: Ravi Kumar
    email: rkravi365@gmail.com
version: 0.4.0
date-released: 2026-11-08
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/erw-del/hetero1d"
url: "https://pypi.org/project/hetero1d/"
keywords:
  - semiconductor heterostructures
  - quantum wells
  - Schrödinger equation
  - effective mass
  - strain
  - optical gain
  - Python
